wine11 : synchronisation en process sur macOS (memoire partagee + attente par adresse)

Wine 11.18 possede deja une synchronisation « en process » (inproc sync) : le
serveur cree chaque evenement, mutex ou semaphore -- et la synchro interne de
chaque processus, fil, minuterie, fichier, file de messages -- comme un objet
du pilote Linux ntsync, en passe le descripteur aux clients, et ceux-ci
l'operent par ioctl sans parler au serveur (dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c,
server/inproc_sync.c). macOS n'a pas ce pilote : HAVE_LINUX_NTSYNC_H est
indefini, tout passe par le socket wineserver, et sur Expedition 33 le
RenderThread passe 21 % de son temps a attendre la reponse du serveur pour
NtSetEvent/NtWaitForSingleObject (profil-renderthread.md), le GameThread 58 %.

Ce correctif ajoute un troisieme backend, macOS seulement, derriere les memes
points d'entree : le serveur cree UN fichier de memoire partagee (64 Mio
creux, dans son repertoire, supprime aussitot, le descripteur circule par
init_first_thread comme le device ntsync) decoupe en cases de 64 octets ;
chaque objet inproc est une case (include/wine/cidre_sync.h). Clients et
serveur modifient l'etat par atomiques et dorment ou reveillent par adresse :
os_sync_wait_on_address / os_sync_wake_by_address avec le drapeau SHARED,
verifie comme traversant les processus (tests/sonde_sync_xproc.c ; le drapeau
NONE ne traverse pas). Le serveur alloue les cases, pose l'etat initial,
signale/remet a zero les evenements internes, abandonne les mutex d'un fil
mort ; il n'attend jamais. Le protocole change (962 -> 963) : la reponse de
get_inproc_sync_fd et de get_inproc_alert_fd porte l'index et la generation
de la case au lieu d'envoyer un descripteur.

Attente sur plusieurs objets : un fil ne dort que sur une adresse ; sa case
d'alerte APC (que le serveur cree deja par fil) lui sert d'oreiller
(wake_seq) ; il s'inscrit dans la table waiter[8] de chaque objet, et qui
change l'etat d'un objet reveille les inscrits. Table pleine = scrutation par
tranches de 1 ms (rare : plus de 8 fils en attente multiple sur un meme
objet). Vie d'une case : le serveur compte les jetons distribues (refs) ; la
case d'un objet detruit encore tenue par des clients devient orpheline,
reste valide (attente sur handle ferme, mutex orphelin abandonne a la mort
du proprietaire, comme ntsync) et est reprise quand refs retombe a 0.

Desactive par defaut : le serveur n'active le backend que s'il demarre avec
CIDRE_SYNC_LOCAL=1 (sinon rien ne change, hormis les deux champs de reponse
a zero). CIDRE_SYNC_STATS=1 imprime a la sortie de chaque processus des
compteurs silencieux (appels NtSetEvent/NtWait..., sommeils, reveils avec
syscall, attentes multiples, scrutation, jetons perimes), dans les deux modes.

Mesure (tests/banc_sync.c, x86_64 emule, M1 Max, prefixe a part) : SetEvent
sans waiter 5,5 us -> 0,05 us ; WaitForSingleObject deja signale 7,1 -> 0,06 ;
SetEvent auto + Wait 12,2 -> 0,12 ; mutex prendre+rendre 11,9 -> 0,12 ;
WaitForMultipleObjects(2) 13,4 -> 0,14 ; ping-pong entre deux fils 22,7 ->
8,1 us par tour. Validation : kernel32:sync (3440 lignes, 347 k tests)
meme resultat qu'avant (1 echec preexistant, todo), tests/test_sync_xproc.c
(35 cas : evenements et semaphores nommes signales depuis un autre processus,
mutex abandonne a la mort d'un processus, attente de processus et de fil,
minuterie, APC, MsgWait, 24 fils en attente multiple, wait-all, 64 objets,
PulseEvent) tout bon dans les deux modes.

Liberation a la Windows : SetEvent libere tous les fils qui attendaient a cet
instant meme si ResetEvent suit aussitot (PulseEvent ne fait que cela) ;
esync, fsync et msync perdent ce reveil (le fil relit l'etat apres la remise a
zero et se rendort). Ici chaque signal incremente une generation par objet et
un fil declare dormeur qui la voit changer est libere. Garde-fou : une attente
infinie se reveille toutes les 2 s pour reverifier ; un objet trouve pris sans
reveil est compte (« reveils manques ») et signale (ERR, 10 fois au plus).
CIDRE_SYNC_STATS=2 imprime aussi les compteurs toutes les 60 s.

Limites connues : wait-all par prise groupee avec restitution
si un autre fil a ete plus rapide (pas atomique comme ntsync) ; un processus
qui meurt sans rendre ses jetons laisse ses cases orphelines perdues (bornee
par ses objets) ; 1 M de cases au plus. Licence LGPL 2.1+, code ecrit a
partir des sources Wine ; msync (CrossOver, LGPL) a servi de reference de
conception, aucun code repris.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index fe7611e4..6f37a9df 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -1694,10 +1694,20 @@ void server_init_process( struct thread_data *data )
             startup_info_size = reply->info_size;
             server_start_time = reply->server_start;
             supported_machines_count = wine_server_reply_size( reply ) / sizeof(*supported_machines);
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+            cidre_sync_init_stats();
+#endif
             if (reply->inproc_device)
             {
                 inproc_device_fd = wine_server_receive_fd( &handle );
                 assert( handle == reply->inproc_device );
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+                if (!cidre_sync_map( inproc_device_fd ))   /* memoire partagee de la synchro en process */
+                {
+                    close( inproc_device_fd );
+                    inproc_device_fd = -1;
+                }
+#endif
             }
         }
     }
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
index 085d5189..0ae2b2d0 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
@@ -77,6 +77,15 @@ WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(sync);
 HANDLE keyed_event = 0;
 int inproc_device_fd = -1;
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+/* Compteurs silencieux de la synchronisation (Cidre) : CIDRE_SYNC_STATS=1 les imprime a la sortie du processus.
+ * Increments non atomiques, volontairement : un compte approximatif suffit, et il ne doit rien couter. */
+unsigned int cidre_sync_stats[CIDRE_STAT_COUNT];
+#define CIDRE_STAT(n) (cidre_sync_stats[CIDRE_STAT_##n]++)
+#else
+#define CIDRE_STAT(n) do {} while (0)
+#endif
+
 static const char *debugstr_timeout( const LARGE_INTEGER *timeout )
 {
     if (!timeout) return "(infinite)";
@@ -449,6 +458,539 @@ static NTSTATUS linux_wait_objs( int device, DWORD count, const int *objs, WAIT_
     return errno_to_status( errno );
 }
 
+#elif defined(__APPLE__) && defined(MAC_OS_VERSION_14_4)
+/*
+ * Cidre : synchronisation en process par memoire partagee (macOS). Le serveur
+ * alloue une case de 64 octets par objet (include/wine/cidre_sync.h) ; ici on
+ * opere l'etat par atomiques et on dort par adresse (drapeau SHARED : traverse
+ * les processus). Le « fd » d'un objet est un jeton : index de case (20 bits)
+ * + generation (11 bits), verifie a chaque operation.
+ */
+#define CIDRE_SYNC_SHM 1
+
+#include <sys/mman.h>
+#include "wine/cidre_sync.h"
+
+static struct cidre_sync_slot *shm_slots;
+static int get_inproc_alert_fd(void);
+
+#define SHM_INDEX(tok)  ((unsigned int)(tok) & 0xfffff)
+#define SHM_GEN(tok)    (((unsigned int)(tok) >> 20) & 0x7ff)   /* 11 bits : le jeton reste positif */
+#define SHM_WAIT_FLAGS  OS_SYNC_WAIT_ON_ADDRESS_SHARED
+#define SHM_WAKE_FLAGS  OS_SYNC_WAKE_BY_ADDRESS_SHARED
+#define SHM_POLL_NS     1000000   /* scrutation quand la table d'inscription d'un objet est pleine */
+
+static inline int shm_token( unsigned int index, unsigned int generation )
+{
+    return index | ((generation & 0x7ff) << 20);
+}
+
+/* appele par server.c a la reception du descripteur de la memoire partagee */
+BOOL cidre_sync_map( int fd )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_header *hdr;
+    void *ptr;
+
+    if (__builtin_available( macOS 14.4, * )) {}
+    else return FALSE;
+
+    ptr = mmap( NULL, (size_t)CIDRE_SYNC_MAX_SLOTS * CIDRE_SYNC_SLOT_SIZE, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, fd, 0 );
+    if (ptr == MAP_FAILED) return FALSE;
+    hdr = ptr;
+    if (__atomic_load_n( &hdr->magic, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) != CIDRE_SYNC_MAGIC)
+    {
+        munmap( ptr, (size_t)CIDRE_SYNC_MAX_SLOTS * CIDRE_SYNC_SLOT_SIZE );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+    shm_slots = ptr;
+    TRACE( "synchronisation en process activee (memoire partagee %p)\n", ptr );
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+static void cidre_sync_dump_stats(void)
+{
+    static const char *names[CIDRE_STAT_COUNT] = { "NtSetEvent", "NtResetEvent", "NtReleaseSemaphore", "NtReleaseMutant",
+        "NtWaitForMultipleObjects", "NtWaitForSingleObject", "NtSignalAndWait", "sommeils (os_sync_wait)",
+        "reveils avec syscall", "attentes multiples/alertables", "tours en scrutation", "jetons perimes",
+        "reveils manques (garde-fou 2 s)" };
+    unsigned int i;
+    fprintf( stderr, "cidre sync stats (pid %u, %s) :\n", getpid(), shm_slots ? "en process" : "wineserver" );
+    for (i = 0; i < CIDRE_STAT_COUNT; i++) fprintf( stderr, "  %-32s %u\n", names[i], cidre_sync_stats[i] );
+}
+
+static ULONGLONG shm_now_ns( clockid_t clock );
+static ULONGLONG cidre_stats_next_dump;   /* CIDRE_SYNC_STATS=2 : aussi toutes les 60 s (un gel tue le processus avant la sortie) */
+
+void cidre_sync_init_stats(void)
+{
+    const char *env = getenv( "CIDRE_SYNC_STATS" );
+    if (!env || !*env || !strcmp( env, "0" )) return;
+    atexit( cidre_sync_dump_stats );
+    if (atoi( env ) >= 2) cidre_stats_next_dump = shm_now_ns( CLOCK_MONOTONIC ) + 60ull * NSECPERSEC;
+}
+
+static void cidre_sync_periodic_stats(void)
+{
+    ULONGLONG now, next = cidre_stats_next_dump;
+    if (!next) return;
+    now = shm_now_ns( CLOCK_MONOTONIC );
+    if (now < next) return;
+    if (__atomic_compare_exchange_n( &cidre_stats_next_dump, &next, now + 60ull * NSECPERSEC, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ))
+        cidre_sync_dump_stats();
+}
+
+/* la case d'un jeton, ou NULL si la case a ete liberee ou reallouee depuis */
+static struct cidre_sync_slot *shm_slot( int tok )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+
+    if (!shm_slots || !SHM_INDEX(tok) || SHM_INDEX(tok) >= CIDRE_SYNC_MAX_SLOTS) return NULL;
+    slot = &shm_slots[SHM_INDEX(tok)];
+    if ((__atomic_load_n( &slot->generation, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) & 0x7ff) != SHM_GEN(tok)) { CIDRE_STAT( STALE ); return NULL; }
+    return slot;
+}
+
+/* le cache lache ce jeton : la case peut etre reprise par le serveur si son objet a deja disparu */
+static void shm_drop_ref( int tok )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+    if ((slot = shm_slot( tok ))) __atomic_sub_fetch( &slot->refs, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+}
+
+/* reveille ce qui dort sur une case : les attentes directes sur &state, puis les attentes multiples inscrites */
+static void shm_wake( struct cidre_sync_slot *slot, int all )
+{
+    unsigned int i, idx;
+
+    __atomic_add_fetch( &slot->wake_seq, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );   /* generation de liberation */
+    if (__atomic_load_n( &slot->waiters, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ))
+    {
+        CIDRE_STAT( WAKE_SYSCALL );
+        if (all) os_sync_wake_by_address_all( &slot->state, 4, SHM_WAKE_FLAGS );
+        else os_sync_wake_by_address_any( &slot->state, 4, SHM_WAKE_FLAGS );
+    }
+    for (i = 0; i < CIDRE_SYNC_WAITER_SLOTS; i++)
+    {
+        if (!(idx = __atomic_load_n( &slot->waiter[i], __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )) || idx >= CIDRE_SYNC_MAX_SLOTS) continue;
+        CIDRE_STAT( WAKE_SYSCALL );
+        __atomic_add_fetch( &shm_slots[idx].wake_seq, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+        os_sync_wake_by_address_all( &shm_slots[idx].wake_seq, 4, SHM_WAKE_FLAGS );
+    }
+}
+
+/* dort tant que *addr == value ; 0 = infini ; rend 0, ou -1 avec errno (ETIMEDOUT, EINTR...) */
+static int shm_wait( unsigned int *addr, unsigned int value, ULONGLONG remaining_ns )
+{
+    CIDRE_STAT( SLEEP );
+    cidre_sync_periodic_stats();
+    if (!remaining_ns) return os_sync_wait_on_address( addr, value, 4, SHM_WAIT_FLAGS );
+    return os_sync_wait_on_address_with_timeout( addr, value, 4, SHM_WAIT_FLAGS, OS_CLOCK_MACH_ABSOLUTE_TIME, remaining_ns );
+}
+
+static ULONGLONG shm_now_ns( clockid_t clock )
+{
+    struct timespec ts;
+    clock_gettime( clock, &ts );
+    return (ULONGLONG)ts.tv_sec * NSECPERSEC + ts.tv_nsec;
+}
+
+struct shm_deadline
+{
+    int       infinite;
+    clockid_t clock;
+    ULONGLONG when;   /* ns sur l'horloge choisie */
+};
+
+static void shm_deadline_init( struct shm_deadline *dl, const LARGE_INTEGER *timeout )
+{
+    if (!timeout || timeout->QuadPart == TIMEOUT_INFINITE) { dl->infinite = 1; return; }
+    dl->infinite = 0;
+    if (timeout->QuadPart <= 0)
+    {
+        dl->clock = CLOCK_MONOTONIC;
+        dl->when = shm_now_ns( CLOCK_MONOTONIC ) + (ULONGLONG)(-timeout->QuadPart) * 100;
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        dl->clock = CLOCK_REALTIME;
+        dl->when = (ULONGLONG)timeout->QuadPart * 100 - (ULONGLONG)SECS_1601_TO_1970 * NSECPERSEC;
+    }
+}
+
+/* temps restant en ns ; 0 = infini ; rend FALSE si echu */
+static BOOL shm_deadline_remaining( const struct shm_deadline *dl, ULONGLONG *remaining )
+{
+    ULONGLONG now;
+
+    if (dl->infinite) { *remaining = 0; return TRUE; }
+    now = shm_now_ns( dl->clock );
+    if (now >= dl->when) return FALSE;
+    *remaining = dl->when - now;
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_release_semaphore_obj( int obj, ULONG count, ULONG *prev_count )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+    unsigned int cur, max;
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    max = slot->aux;
+    cur = __atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    do
+    {
+        if (count > max - cur) return STATUS_SEMAPHORE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED;
+    } while (!__atomic_compare_exchange_n( &slot->state, &cur, cur + count, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ));
+    if (prev_count) *prev_count = cur;
+    if (count && !cur) shm_wake( slot, count > 1 );
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_query_semaphore_obj( int obj, SEMAPHORE_BASIC_INFORMATION *info )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    info->CurrentCount = __atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    info->MaximumCount = slot->aux;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_set_event_obj( int obj, LONG *prev_state )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+    unsigned int prev;
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    prev = __atomic_exchange_n( &slot->state, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    if (!prev) shm_wake( slot, slot->aux != 0 );
+    if (prev_state) *prev_state = prev;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_reset_event_obj( int obj, LONG *prev_state )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+    unsigned int prev;
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    prev = __atomic_exchange_n( &slot->state, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    if (prev_state) *prev_state = prev;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/* signale, reveille, remet a zero : les fils deja declares dormeurs sont liberes par la generation (voir cidre_sync.h) */
+static NTSTATUS linux_pulse_event_obj( int obj, LONG *prev_state )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+    unsigned int prev, one = 1;
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    prev = __atomic_exchange_n( &slot->state, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    shm_wake( slot, 1 );
+    __atomic_compare_exchange_n( &slot->state, &one, 0, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    if (prev_state) *prev_state = prev;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_query_event_obj( int obj, EVENT_BASIC_INFORMATION *info )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    info->EventType = slot->aux ? NotificationEvent : SynchronizationEvent;
+    info->EventState = __atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_release_mutex_obj( int obj, LONG *prev_count )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+    unsigned int count, tid = GetCurrentThreadId();
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    if (__atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) != tid) return STATUS_MUTANT_NOT_OWNED;
+    count = slot->aux;   /* seul le proprietaire touche aux */
+    if (prev_count) *prev_count = 1 - count;
+    if (count > 1) slot->aux = count - 1;
+    else
+    {
+        slot->aux = 0;
+        __atomic_store_n( &slot->state, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+        shm_wake( slot, 0 );
+    }
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_query_mutex_obj( int obj, MUTANT_BASIC_INFORMATION *info )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slot;
+    unsigned int owner;
+
+    if (!(slot = shm_slot( obj ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    if (__atomic_load_n( &slot->flags, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) & CIDRE_SYNC_ABANDONED)
+    {
+        info->AbandonedState = TRUE;
+        info->OwnedByCaller = FALSE;
+        info->CurrentCount = 1;
+        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
+    owner = __atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    info->AbandonedState = FALSE;
+    info->OwnedByCaller = (owner == GetCurrentThreadId());
+    info->CurrentCount = owner ? 1 - slot->aux : 1;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/* tente de prendre l'objet ; 1 = pris (abandoned pose pour un mutex abandonne), 0 = indisponible et *observed = valeur vue */
+static int shm_try_acquire( struct cidre_sync_slot *slot, unsigned int tid, int *abandoned, unsigned int *observed )
+{
+    unsigned int v = __atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+
+    switch (__atomic_load_n( &slot->flags, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) & CIDRE_SYNC_TYPE_MASK)
+    {
+    case INPROC_SYNC_INTERNAL:
+    case INPROC_SYNC_EVENT:
+        if (!v) { *observed = 0; return 0; }
+        if (slot->aux) return 1;   /* manuel : non consomme */
+        if (__atomic_compare_exchange_n( &slot->state, &v, 0, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )) return 1;
+        *observed = 0;   /* consomme par un autre entre-temps */
+        return 0;
+
+    case INPROC_SYNC_SEMAPHORE:
+        while (v)
+            if (__atomic_compare_exchange_n( &slot->state, &v, v - 1, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )) return 1;
+        *observed = 0;
+        return 0;
+
+    case INPROC_SYNC_MUTEX:
+        if (v == tid) { slot->aux++; return 1; }
+        if (!v && __atomic_compare_exchange_n( &slot->state, &v, tid, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ))
+        {
+            slot->aux = 1;
+            if (__atomic_load_n( &slot->flags, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) & CIDRE_SYNC_ABANDONED)
+            {
+                __atomic_and_fetch( &slot->flags, ~CIDRE_SYNC_ABANDONED, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+                *abandoned = 1;
+            }
+            return 1;
+        }
+        *observed = v;   /* v est le proprietaire courant (non nul : le CAS n'echoue que si quelqu'un l'a pris) */
+        return 0;
+    }
+    *observed = v;
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* un evenement manuel (ou interne) libere par generation : tout dormeur present au signal est satisfait */
+static inline int shm_releases_by_generation( const struct cidre_sync_slot *slot )
+{
+    unsigned int type = __atomic_load_n( &slot->flags, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) & CIDRE_SYNC_TYPE_MASK;
+    return (type == INPROC_SYNC_EVENT || type == INPROC_SYNC_INTERNAL) && slot->aux;
+}
+
+#define SHM_WATCHDOG_NS 2000000000ull   /* garde-fou : une attente infinie se reveille toutes les 2 s pour revérifier */
+
+/* l'objet serait-il pris par tid sans attendre ? (WaitAll : verification avant la prise groupee) */
+static int shm_is_available( struct cidre_sync_slot *slot, unsigned int tid )
+{
+    unsigned int v = __atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+
+    if ((__atomic_load_n( &slot->flags, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) & CIDRE_SYNC_TYPE_MASK) == INPROC_SYNC_MUTEX)
+        return !v || v == tid;
+    return v != 0;
+}
+
+/* rend ce qu'une prise groupee avait pris avant d'echouer */
+static void shm_undo_acquire( struct cidre_sync_slot *slot, unsigned int tid )
+{
+    switch (__atomic_load_n( &slot->flags, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) & CIDRE_SYNC_TYPE_MASK)
+    {
+    case INPROC_SYNC_INTERNAL:
+    case INPROC_SYNC_EVENT:
+        if (slot->aux) break;
+        if (!__atomic_exchange_n( &slot->state, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )) shm_wake( slot, 0 );
+        break;
+    case INPROC_SYNC_SEMAPHORE:
+        if (!__atomic_fetch_add( &slot->state, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )) shm_wake( slot, 0 );
+        break;
+    case INPROC_SYNC_MUTEX:
+        if (slot->aux > 1) slot->aux--;
+        else
+        {
+            slot->aux = 0;
+            __atomic_store_n( &slot->state, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+            shm_wake( slot, 0 );
+        }
+        break;
+    }
+}
+
+/* le garde-fou a trouve l'objet pris alors qu'aucun reveil n'est arrive : compte et dit le type (10 fois au plus) */
+static void shm_late_wake( struct cidre_sync_slot *slot )
+{
+    static LONG dits;
+    CIDRE_STAT( LATE_WAKE );
+    if (InterlockedIncrement( &dits ) <= 10)
+        ERR( "reveil manque rattrape par le garde-fou : case %u type %u manuel %u etat %u waiters %u\n",
+             (unsigned int)(slot - shm_slots), slot->flags & CIDRE_SYNC_TYPE_MASK, slot->aux,
+             __atomic_load_n( &slot->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ), __atomic_load_n( &slot->waiters, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) );
+}
+
+/* inscription d'un fil (sa case = me) dans la table d'un objet ; rend l'emplacement + 1, ou 0 si pleine */
+static int shm_register( struct cidre_sync_slot *slot, unsigned int me )
+{
+    unsigned int i, zero;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < CIDRE_SYNC_WAITER_SLOTS; i++)
+    {
+        zero = 0;
+        if (__atomic_compare_exchange_n( &slot->waiter[i], &zero, me, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )) return i + 1;
+    }
+    __atomic_add_fetch( &slot->overflow, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void shm_unregister( struct cidre_sync_slot *slot, int where, unsigned int me )
+{
+    unsigned int expected = me;
+    if (where) __atomic_compare_exchange_n( &slot->waiter[where - 1], &expected, 0, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS linux_wait_objs( int device, DWORD count, const int *objs, WAIT_TYPE type,
+                                 int alert_fd, const LARGE_INTEGER *timeout )
+{
+    struct cidre_sync_slot *slots[MAXIMUM_WAIT_OBJECTS + 1], *me = NULL;
+    int registered[MAXIMUM_WAIT_OBJECTS + 1];
+    unsigned int gens[MAXIMUM_WAIT_OBJECTS + 1];
+    unsigned int tid = GetCurrentThreadId(), total = count, i, me_index = 0;
+    struct shm_deadline dl;
+    ULONGLONG remaining;
+    int polling = 0, abandoned = 0, late = 0;
+    NTSTATUS ret;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+        if (!(slots[i] = shm_slot( objs[i] ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+    if (alert_fd)
+    {
+        if (!(slots[total] = shm_slot( alert_fd ))) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
+        total++;
+    }
+    shm_deadline_init( &dl, timeout );
+
+    /* chemin rapide : un seul objet, pas d'alerte : on dort directement sur son mot d'etat */
+    if (total == 1)
+    {
+        struct cidre_sync_slot *slot = slots[0];
+        unsigned int observed;
+        int rc;
+
+        int by_gen = shm_releases_by_generation( slot ), watchdog;
+        unsigned int gen;
+
+        for (;;)
+        {
+            gen = __atomic_load_n( &slot->wake_seq, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+            if (shm_try_acquire( slot, tid, &abandoned, &observed )) return abandoned ? STATUS_ABANDONED : STATUS_SUCCESS;
+            if (!shm_deadline_remaining( &dl, &remaining )) return STATUS_TIMEOUT;
+            watchdog = !remaining || remaining > SHM_WATCHDOG_NS;
+            if (watchdog) remaining = SHM_WATCHDOG_NS;
+            __atomic_add_fetch( &slot->waiters, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+            /* dormeur declare : un signal arrive entre-temps nous libere (generation) ou nous reveille (waiters vu) */
+            if (by_gen && __atomic_load_n( &slot->wake_seq, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) != gen) rc = 0;
+            else rc = shm_wait( &slot->state, observed, remaining );
+            __atomic_sub_fetch( &slot->waiters, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+            if (!shm_slot( objs[0] )) return STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;   /* liberee pendant l'attente */
+            if (by_gen && __atomic_load_n( &slot->wake_seq, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) != gen) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+            if (rc < 0 && errno == ETIMEDOUT)
+            {
+                if (shm_try_acquire( slot, tid, &abandoned, &observed ))
+                {
+                    if (watchdog) shm_late_wake( slot );
+                    return abandoned ? STATUS_ABANDONED : STATUS_SUCCESS;
+                }
+                if (!watchdog) return STATUS_TIMEOUT;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /* plusieurs objets (ou alerte) : on s'inscrit chez chacun et on dort sur sa propre case */
+    CIDRE_STAT( MULTI );
+    me_index = SHM_INDEX( get_inproc_alert_fd() );
+    if (me_index && me_index < CIDRE_SYNC_MAX_SLOTS) me = &shm_slots[me_index];
+    if (!me) polling = 1;   /* pas de case propre : scrutation lente */
+
+    for (i = 0; i < total; i++)
+    {
+        registered[i] = me ? shm_register( slots[i], me_index ) : 0;
+        if (!registered[i]) polling = 1;
+    }
+
+    for (i = 0; i < count; i++) gens[i] = __atomic_load_n( &slots[i]->wake_seq, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+
+    for (;;)
+    {
+        unsigned int seq = me ? __atomic_load_n( &me->wake_seq, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) : 0, observed;
+        int rc, watchdog;
+
+        if (type != WaitAll)
+        {
+            for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+            {
+                if (!shm_try_acquire( slots[i], tid, &abandoned, &observed ))
+                {
+                    /* evenement manuel signale puis remis a zero pendant notre attente : nous etions a liberer */
+                    if (!(shm_releases_by_generation( slots[i] ) &&
+                          __atomic_load_n( &slots[i]->wake_seq, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST ) != gens[i])) continue;
+                }
+                if (late) shm_late_wake( slots[i] );
+                ret = abandoned ? STATUS_ABANDONED + i : i;
+                goto done;
+            }
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            for (i = 0; i < count; i++) if (!shm_is_available( slots[i], tid )) break;
+            if (i == count)
+            {
+                for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+                    if (!shm_try_acquire( slots[i], tid, &abandoned, &observed )) break;
+                if (i == count) { if (late) shm_late_wake( slots[0] ); ret = abandoned ? STATUS_ABANDONED : STATUS_SUCCESS; goto done; }
+                while (i--) shm_undo_acquire( slots[i], tid );   /* un autre a ete plus rapide : on rend et on reessaie */
+                continue;
+            }
+        }
+        if (alert_fd && __atomic_load_n( &slots[count]->state, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )) { ret = count; goto done; }
+
+        if (!shm_deadline_remaining( &dl, &remaining )) { ret = STATUS_TIMEOUT; goto done; }
+        watchdog = !remaining || remaining > SHM_WATCHDOG_NS;
+        if (watchdog) remaining = SHM_WATCHDOG_NS;
+        if (polling && remaining > SHM_POLL_NS) { remaining = SHM_POLL_NS; CIDRE_STAT( POLL ); }
+        if (me) rc = shm_wait( &me->wake_seq, seq, remaining );
+        else
+        {
+            struct timespec ts = { 0, SHM_POLL_NS };
+            nanosleep( &ts, NULL );
+            rc = 0;
+        }
+        late = (watchdog && !polling && rc < 0 && errno == ETIMEDOUT);   /* personne ne nous a reveilles : si un objet est pris, c'est un reveil manque */
+
+        for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+            if (!shm_slot( objs[i] )) { ret = STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE; goto done; }
+    }
+
+done:
+    for (i = 0; i < total; i++) shm_unregister( slots[i], registered[i], me_index );
+    if (ret == count && alert_fd)
+    {
+        static const LARGE_INTEGER zero;
+        ret = server_wait( NULL, 0, SELECT_INTERRUPTIBLE | SELECT_ALERTABLE, &zero );
+        assert( ret == STATUS_USER_APC );
+        return ret;
+    }
+    return ret;
+}
